--- !u!114 &205117622
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 205117620}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<size=100><color=red>Welcome to The Engineer's Arena</color></size>\r\n\r\nThis
    tutorial will quickly and simply teach you everything you need to know to play
    the game. If you ever forget something, don\u2019t worry, you can access the
    tutorial anytime from any part of the game.\r\n\r\nIf you're not sure what this
    game is about, let me explain. The Engineer\u2019s Arena is a fun and competitive
    game designed for you and a friend. You\u2019ll pick unique parts for your robot,
    program its controls (or use default ones if coding isn't your thing), and choose
    between button or camera-based input. Once you're ready (don\u2019t worry, once
    you get used to it, this part takes just a few seconds), the battle begins! You
    and your friend will compete on various maps in a best-of-five match, testing
    your decision-making and control skills. After each game, you\u2019ll earn XP,
    level up, and climb the global leaderboard. There\u2019s also a single-player
    mode for practice and level grinding when you're playing alone.\r\n\r\n<color=red>This
    app serves only as a controller. To play the game, you\u2019ll also need a Windows
    computer where you can install The Engineer\u2019s Arena (PC version) from https://sumskivrac.itch.io/the-engeni.
    Your computer will act as the server, running the actual game. You also need
    to make sure that you, the PC and your friend, if you are playing multiplayer,
    are all on same Wi-Fi network.\r\n\r\nAs you can see, the tutorial is divided
    into nine sections. If this is your first time playing, I recommend reading them
    in order, from left to right and then down.</color>\r\n\r\nI hope you have fun
    and enjoy the game. Good luck, soldier!\r\n\r\n<color=red>-The Developer-</color>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 32e9087bea9953c46ab22aa5c5c10950, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 9016579006585588636, guid: 32e9087bea9953c46ab22aa5c5c10950, type: 2}
