--- !u!114 &1020246021
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1020246019}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<size=100><color=red>Battle Explanation</color></size>\r\n\r\nThis section
    of the tutorial explains the main part of the game: battles.\r\n\r\nOn your phone,
    controls remain the same as explained in the Input section of the tutorial. However,
    on the server, many things are happening in real time to make battles dynamic
    and engaging.\r\n\r\nOnce you select your input method, the battle will begin.\r\nIn
    multiplayer, both players must be ready before the fight starts.\r\nIn singleplayer,
    you will face an AI opponent, designed mostly for practice. While the AI isn\u2019t
    too advanced, underestimating it can cost you the match.\r\n\r\nYou and your
    opponent fight until one of you is destroyed.\r\nThe game is played to five wins,
    meaning a match can last up to nine rounds max.\r\nEverything resets after each
    round, so even if you lose one fight, you\u2019ll get another chance to win the
    match.\r\n\r\n<color=red>Each round, a random map is chosen.\r\nMost maps have
    unique characteristics, making battles both funny and strategic.\r\nIf you struggle
    on one map, you might perform better on another.\r\nInteractive Map Elements\r\nSome
    maps include special objects that you can interact with, for example:\r\nPoison
    Bushes \u2013 Touch them, and your robot will take damage.\r\nAttacking Octopuses
    \u2013 They strike nearby robots.\r\nStinging Jellyfish \u2013 Electric shocks
    that deal damage.\r\nHealing Shells \u2013 Restores a small amount of health.\r\nBreaking
    Ice \u2013 Parts of the map may collapse under pressure.\r\nDeadly Hooks \u2013
    Pulls robots off the battlefield and destroy them.\r\nAbducting UFOs \u2013 Can
    lift robots and drop them elsewhere.\r\n...</color>\r\nTo dominate the game,
    you\u2019ll need to learn the maps and develop strategies for each one!"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 32e9087bea9953c46ab22aa5c5c10950, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 9016579006585588636, guid: 32e9087bea9953c46ab22aa5c5c10950, type: 2}
