--- !u!114 &1110569900
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1110569898}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<size=100><color=red>Credits</color></size>\n\nHi, glad to see you here!\n\nMy
    name is Nikola, and I\u2019m a software engineering student from Serbia and the
    developer of this game.\n\nEverything you see in this game was made by me:\nEvery
    line of code\nEvery pixel of art\nEvery aspect of game design\nThis game started
    as a fun project, something I put together in less than a month. I love experimenting
    with new things, but let's be honest, programming can sometimes be boring. Writing
    thousands of lines of code just to make a dull application isn't very exciting.
    That\u2019s why I turn my experiments into games, to create something fun and
    lasting from my code.\n\nThis game was originally just an experiment with Wi-Fi
    multiplayer and camera detection, but it ended up becoming a full game.\n\nThis
    is my first officially released game, though I have many others in development.
    The reason this one made it out first is that it was the fastest to complete.\n\nI
    know the game doesn\u2019t have a ton of content yet, and there are probably
    a few rare bugs (hopefully, you didn\u2019t find them \U0001F605. <color=red>Robot
    stuck? Press R to reset</color>). Right now, I need to focus on my other projects,
    but if this game gets even a little recognition, I\u2019d love to add more features,
    polish it further, and fix any remaining issues.\n\nI truly hope you enjoyed
    the game and had a fun experience.\nThank you for playing The Engineer's Arena!\n\n-
    The Developer-"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
