  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<size=100><color=red>Connection Explanation</color></size>\n\nConnection
    is a simple process, once you get used to it, you won\u2019t even notice it.
    However, in the background, it serves as the core of the game, keeping battles
    active. Because of its importance, it definitely deserves its own section in
    the tutorial.\n\nTo start a game, you need to connect to a server. If you\u2019re
    playing multiplayer, your friend must also connect. You do this by pressing Play
    both here and on the server. Don\u2019t worry too much, both your phone and the
    server will indicate whether you are connected or not.\n\n<color=red>Here\u2019s
    the most important part about connection:</color>\nTo connect to the server,
    you must be on the same Wi-Fi network as the server. If you\u2019re unable to
    connect even after setting the same network, there may be a minor issue, and
    restarting both the app and server will likely fix it.\n\nIf you\u2019ve restarted
    multiple times and confirmed that you are on the same network, then there might
    be a PC settings issue. The most common cause is Windows Firewall.\n\nWhen connecting
    for the first time, you should see a prompt asking whether to allow the game
    through the firewall. You must allow the connection, as the game requires Wi-Fi
    for battles.\n\nIf you accidentally blocked the connection or didn\u2019t see
    the prompt, you\u2019ll need to manually go to Windows Firewall settings and
    allow the server to access the network.\n\nIf the issue persists, your antivirus
    software may be blocking the connection. Try disabling it temporarily or adding
    an exception for the game."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 32e9087bea9953c46ab22aa5c5c10950, type: 2}
