--- !u!114 &1711631334
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1711631332}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<size=100><color=red>Controls Explanation</color></size>\r\n\r\nThis section
    of the tutorial explains the game\u2019s controls.\r\nThere are two types of
    controls in the game: default and custom.\r\n\r\n<color=red>Default Controls</color>\r\nIf
    you choose default controls, you don\u2019t need to worry about this section.
    The game will use a pre-set layout of functions, so you won\u2019t have to configure
    anything. However, you won\u2019t be able to customize the layout to your preferences.\r\n\r\n<color=red>Custom
    Controls</color>\r\nCustom controls are more complex but offer complete flexibility.
    Instead of using a preset layout, you start with an empty control setup and must
    manually assign functions to controls.\r\nIn the game, controls are assigned
    to colors. There are five different colors:\r\n<color=red>Red</color>\r\n<color=green>Green</color>\r\n<color=blue>Blue</color>\r\n<color=white>White</color>\r\n<color=grey>Black</color>\nEach
    function can be assigned to one of these colors.\r\nThere are three types of
    functions:\r\nIf \u2013 Works like a button: When pressed, it performs an action
    once.\r\nWhile \u2013 Works like a switch: It remains active until pressed again.\r\nFor
    \u2013 Works like a hold button: It remains active while being held down.\r\nAssigning
    functions to colors works like this:\r\nSelect a part of the robot. The available
    functions for that part will be displayed.\r\nChoose a function and assign it
    to a color by pressing the desired color.\r\nThe assigned function will appear
    in a generated code preview, showing its type.\r\nTo remove a function, repeat
    the same process and it will be unassigned from the color.\r\nOnce you assign
    the first function to a color, that color\u2019s function type is locked.\r\nYou
    can add more functions to that color, but only if they match the same type (If,
    While, or For).\r\nTo change the function type of a color, you must remove all
    assigned functions first.\r\nAdvantages of Custom Controls:\r\nCustom Layout
    \u2013 Assign functions to the colors that feel most comfortable for you.\r\nAdditional
    Functions \u2013 Two exclusive functions are available in custom controls:\r\nForce
    Cooldown (for melee and ranged weapons)\r\nDemolish (for the robot body)\r\nCustom
    controls allow you to fine-tune your gameplay and optimize your strategy. Whether
    you use them or not is entirely up to you!"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 32e9087bea9953c46ab22aa5c5c10950, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 9016579006585588636, guid: 32e9087bea9953c46ab22aa5c5c10950, type: 2}
